# DeOpt v2 frontend — LOCAL DEV ENVIRONMENT TEMPLATE
#
# Posture: localhost dev only. Public testnet beta (Base Sepolia).
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) for local use; do NOT commit real
# values. **NEVER mainnet.**

# --- Trading API base URL (public reads against the backend) ---
# Default points at the local backend started by
# `scripts/local-backend.sh`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TRADING_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# --- Expected chain ---
# Refuses to default to mainnet (see `src/lib/chains.ts`); always
# Sepolia in this beta.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ENV=sepolia

# --- Admin dashboard backend URL (OPTIONAL) ---
# The /admin route reads this to decide where admin XHRs go. Leave
# UNSET for the public-facing deploy; useful only when you run the
# admin dashboard locally against a backend that has admin endpoints
# enabled. Do NOT paste a real admin bearer token into a browser
# pointed at a public app.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080

# --- Perps ticket enablement (build-time flag) ---
# The public opt-in gate for the Perps trade form. Default false →
# submit button renders hard-disabled with `data-ticket-mode="disabled"`.
# Read at build time via `src/lib/perps-flag.ts::isPerpsTicketEnabled()`.
# This flag is NOT a security control — the backend
# `PERPS_PUBLIC_TRADING_ENABLED` + `PERPS_CLOSED_TEST_ENABLED` gates
# are authoritative. Never set to `true` on a public build without
# operator sign-off.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PERPS_TICKET_ENABLED=false

# --- Perps closed-test informational banner (build-time flag) ---
# Cosmetic-only. When true, the /perps page renders a closed-test
# banner explaining that trading is restricted to allowlisted wallets.
# Does NOT grant access to anything: the backend allowlist is the
# only authority. Read via `src/lib/perps-closed-test-flag.ts`.
#
# When this flag AND `NEXT_PUBLIC_PERPS_TICKET_ENABLED` are BOTH true,
# the perps trade form switches to the SIGNED intent submit path
# (PERPS-FULLSTACK-RUNTIME-INTEGRATION-V1 Part D + H) that posts an
# EIP-712 `PerpOrderIntent` signature to `POST /perps/orders/signed`.
# The backend still 503s if the wallet isn't on the closed-test
# allowlist — this flag is UI copy only.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PERPS_CLOSED_TEST_ENABLED=false

# --- PerpMatchingEngine EIP-712 domain address (build-time) ---
# The on-chain address of the PerpMatchingEngine contract on the
# current chain. This value becomes the `verifyingContract` field in
# the EIP-712 domain that the frontend signs `PerpOrderIntent`
# envelopes against; the backend re-derives the same domain and
# rejects any signature whose recovered signer doesn't match
# `intent.trader`. NO hardcoded fallback — when unset the perps
# signing path refuses to open the wallet prompt rather than sign
# against the zero address on the wrong chain.
# NEVER set to a mainnet contract address without operator sign-off.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PERP_MATCHING_ENGINE_ADDRESS=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

# --- RFQ multi-leg frontend flag (build-time) ---
# Opt-in gate for the multi-leg RFQ path in the RFQ / Strategy
# workspace. Default false → strategies with more than one leg keep
# the existing "backend RFQ is single-leg per RFQ" honest message and
# fire zero network mutation. When true, `state.legs.length > 1`
# routes through `POST /options/multi-leg-rfqs` and the v2 multi-leg
# canonical/authorization pipeline.
#
# This flag is NOT a security control. Backend
# `OPTION_RFQ_MULTI_LEG_ENABLED` is authoritative; a frontend build
# with this flag on will surface an honest 503 disabled message from
# the backend if the backend flag is still off. Never set to `true`
# on a public build without operator sign-off.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RFQ_MULTI_LEG_ENABLED=false
